  "content": "Here is the step-by-step deterministic arithmetic solution.\n\n**Given values:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression to compute:**\n$$ (a \\times b + c^3) - (a - b) \\times c $$\n\n### Step 1: Compute the individual components\n\n**1. Calculate $a \\times b$:**\n$$ 137 \\times 29 $$\nBreakdown:\n$$ 137 \\times 20 = 2740 $$\n$$ 137 \\times 9 = 1233 $$\n$$ 2740 + 1233 = 3973 $$\nSo, **$a \\times b = 3973$**\n\n**2. Calculate $c^3$:**\n$$ 11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 $$\n$$ 11 \\times 11 = 121 $$\n$$ 121 \\times 11 = 1331 $$\nSo, **$c^3 = 1331$**\n\n**3. Calculate $(a \\times b + c^3)$:**\n$$ 3973 + 1331 $$\n$$ 3973 + 1331 = 5304 $$\nSo, **First Part = 5304**\n\n**4. Calculate $(a - b)$:**\n$$ 137 - 29 $$\n$$ 137 - 29 = 108 $$\nSo, **$a - b = 108$**\n\n**5. Calculate $(a - b) \\times c$:**\n$$ 108 \\times 11 $$\nBreakdown:\n$$ 108 \\times 10 = 1080 $$\n$$ 108 \\times 1 = 108 $$\n$$ 1080 + 108 = 1188 $$\nSo, **Second Part = 1188**\n\n### Step 2: Final Subtraction\n\nNow, subtract the Second Part from the First Part:\n$$ 5304 - 11",
